00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:57.049 line:0%
-Hee-hee-hee!
That's a good one, isn't it?

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:58.584 line:0%
-Is it?
-You know what?

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.453 line:0%
[ Laughing ]
That's 100% true.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.121 line:0%
-What?!

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:05.091 line:0%
-I knew it. I knew it.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.893
Really? You threw the baby?

00:02:07.893 --> 00:02:09.662
-And here's what happened.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.832
I mean, we were -- we were
having a picnic up there,

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.668
and then when I noticed --
And I back up to the edge

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.704
after I've gotten rid of the dog
and gotten rid of my son.

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.805
And I grab this little branch
behind me, tree,

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:21.207
and I get behind it.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:24.644
And it's, like, this cherry bush
about as thick as my pinkie.

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.178
I'm like, "This is not
going to save me at all."

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:27.580
And I squared off

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.049
and just tried to go as Yoda
as I could with this ram

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.751
and just say,
"Not me, whatever it is."

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.219
He was kicking dirt
and everything.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:34.754
He hops off the ledge,
swings back around.

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:38.157
We look over on the other side.
His harem is on the other side.

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.293
So we were between him
and all of his ladies,

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:45.398
and he didn't want any other
male scent on his mountain.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.432
-Wow.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.000
-And I was like,
"Your mountain, sir."

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.902
-See? I knew it.
I knew it was true, because --.

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:51.337
-I should have believed it.
-Yeah.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.473
Well, I just --
We have just similar lives.

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:55.808
-Straight out of Brooklyn!

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:59.912
-Here we go. My turn.
Which envelope should I open?

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:01.580
Uh, number one or number two?

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.283
-Oh, yeah, that one. Two.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.252
-You sure?
-That's the one.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:08.887
-This could be the truth
or could be...

00:03:08.887 --> 00:03:11.090
-A lie.
-...a lie. [ Laughs ]

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:16.295
"I once was attacked
by a ram on..."

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:17.763
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:19.799
No, seriously. Here we go.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.569
-It was related to the ram.
-Related to the other ram.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:26.371
Yeah, we were on
vacation together.

00:03:26.371 --> 00:03:29.708
[ Laughs ]
I was dressed as a baby.

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:31.844
Yeah, it was a Dodge Ram

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.612
that had me
cornered in my Airstream.

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:34.813
I was like, "Help!"

00:03:34.813 --> 00:03:36.449
All right. Here we go.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:41.454 line:0%
"I, Jimmy Fallon, once docked
a ferry full of tourists

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.589 line:0%
coming back from
the Statue of Liberty."

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:46.992 line:0%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah?
What year was this?

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:48.694 line:0%
-Yeah, when was this?

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:50.363 line:0%
-I'd say 2000 maybe?

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.764 line:0%
-Did you have a driver's
license back then?

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.966 line:0%
-I do not drive a boat
or anything. No.

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:56.469 line:0%
I had my driver's license, sure.
-Ohh.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.637 line:0%
-And what were you doing coming
from the Statue of Liberty?

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:00.773 line:0%
-I love the Statue of Liberty.
I go there all the time.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:03.109 line:0%
-Just a Saturday, moseying
around, something to do?

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.444 line:0%
-I don't think --
I think it was a weekday.

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:05.945 line:0%
-Were you getting paid
for this job?

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.414 line:0%
-No. No. I just like
the Statue of Liberty.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.849 line:0%
-As the ferryman, or were you
like, "Hey, I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:04:10.849 --> 00:04:14.153 line:0%
Hey, Captain, let me dock
the ferry boat."

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.388 line:0%
-No. I wouldn't do that.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.089 line:0%
I wouldn't put
people's lives in jeopardy.

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:19.325 line:0%
-Who went to the
Statue of Liberty with you?

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:20.826 line:0%
-I went solo.
I went by myself.

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.195 line:0%
-What?!

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:23.896 line:0%
-Oh, it wasn't -- You didn't
have a bunch of tourists

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:25.197 line:0%
that came to see
the Statue of Liberty?

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:26.466 line:0%
-There was
a bunch of people on --

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:27.933 line:0%
-So because you took
the ferry solo by yourself,

00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:29.936 line:0%
a lot of people that really have
never seen the Statue of Liberty

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:32.305 line:0%
had to sit over on land and
wait for you, as a celebrity,

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.606 line:0%
to get back.

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:35.808 line:0%
-No, I didn't go on the boat
by myself, the ferry.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:39.545 line:0%
I went with other people,
but I didn't invite anyone.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.047 line:0%
It wasn't like --
I went by myself.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.748 line:0%
-There were a lot of seats
still open

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:43.849 line:0%
that people were waiting for.

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:45.551 line:0%
-No, no, that's not true.
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.653 line:0%
-Okay. So we can't ask you
any more questions.

00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:50.523 line:0%
-This is a lead-pipe cinch.
-I don't know, man.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:51.857 line:0%
I'm going to say it's a lie.

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:53.059 line:0%
[ Drum roll ]

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.894 line:0%
-You're going to say it's a lie?

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:58.331 line:0%
-Both: It's a lie.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.466 line:0%
-It's true.
-What?!

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.001 line:0%
I drove and docked the ferry.

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:05.371
It was the weirdest thing --
It was the weirdest thing ever.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.640
That is what happened to me.
It was weird. I was coming back.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.608
I went because I really --
I'm into the Statue of Liberty.

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:10.743
It's really amazing.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.545
So I went.
I was just hanging out.

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:15.347
I go, "This is awesome."
Then I get on this ferry back.

00:05:15.347 --> 00:05:16.882
And this captain goes --

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:18.750
People started getting
autographs and stuff like that,

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.053
'cause it was before, like,
cellphones really.

00:05:21.053 --> 00:05:23.356
And so they wanted
autographs and stuff.

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:25.958
And the captain's like, "Just
come up here in the cockpit

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:28.594
and just -- you know,
so you won't get mobbed."

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:29.895
And I go, "Okay."

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:31.864
Then he goes,
"You ever dock a ferry?"

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.332
I go, "What are you
talking about?"

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.701
There's like probably
200 people on this thing.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:37.370
I don't know how many
people fit in a ferry.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.904
I didn't even know
what I was on.

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:40.940
Again, the guy was a great guy.
He's probably fired by now.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.310
-No, yeah, he's not a great guy.
-He's not a great guy.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.579
He's like, "Dude, turn the thing
and pull the throttle

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:47.880
this way and that way."

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.681
And I was like,
"What's going on?"

00:05:49.681 --> 00:05:51.917
And I full-on docked the ferry.

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:53.552
It was absolutely crazy
and totally true.

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:55.087
And I was like,
"What just happened?"

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:56.588
That's what happens
when you hang out

00:05:56.588 --> 00:05:57.723
at the Statue of Liberty.

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:58.957
-Solo.
-Yeah, here we go.

00:05:58.957 --> 00:06:00.359
Solo. All right.
Tariq, here we go.

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.295
-All right. Which one?
